{
    "schemaVersion": 1,
    "written": "2026-10-17",
    "notes": [
        "The first 97 chatter lines, in the ChatterLine shape of directives/spec_living_systems.md section 1.2. Original writing; no published text, no real-world brands, no polity names, no rule or number stated as fact.",
        "Every `when` key is a field of SystemFacts (chatter_schema.md lists them with the source each one is read from). A slot in `text` is resolved from the same facts; a slot that needs a thing (a gas giant, a belt, a moon, a port) carries that thing as a condition, so a line never claims what the system's data contradicts. check_sample.mjs enforces both.",
        "Conditions that look like rules cite the text they come from in chatter_schema.md (the Law Level table, the Atmosphere table, the Starport Facilities table, Bases, Travel Codes, the trade DMs). The lines themselves state nothing as a rule.",
        "weight: 1 unless written. Distress lines are 0.2, so a system hears them rarely.",
        "customs-001, customs-002 and customs-003 are not shipped. Each ties a ban to a Law Level range. Johnny, 2026-10-17 21:10: no line restates a rule. E writes customs lines that ask crews to declare or show papers."
    ],
    "lines": [
